                <pb facs="0762" n="650" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg650"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File 25010/22.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Italian Chargé.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic">June 25,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In view of the fact that Charlton’s arrest, to secure which the preliminary
                    mandate described in article 2 of the convention of 1884 is issued, has, it is
                    reported, already been secured upon the complaint of the Italian consul, and in
                    view of your telegram of June 25, I assume that you are now awaiting
                    instructions from your Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
